# THE CHAT RE-PRESENT HUNT — the sequence a single-step test can never issue.
#
#   dregg-drive --surface telegram --offering tug --as alice --script dregg-drive/scripts/chat-menu.drive
#
# Every command surface here is issued at least TWICE, because the second invocation is the
# one that can EDIT instead of POST. Watch the PAINT line: `SEND` is visible, `EDIT` is only
# visible if that message is still on screen, and a frame with neither is a dead bot.

# ── the command surface, twice each ─────────────────────────────────────────
send /help
send /help
send /offerings
send /offerings
send /offerings

# ── open, twice, then a turn, then open again ──────────────────────────────
open
open
press 0
open

# ── a second offering in the SAME chat: now two live keyboards ─────────────
send /open dungeon
send /offerings
again

# ── the menu after a restart: the buttons on screen are from a dead process ─
restart
send /offerings
stale 0

# ── nonsense on the command surface ───────────────────────────────────────
send /nope
send /open not-a-thing
send /verify
send just talking in the group
send /
controls
